Que 4:- Given the following API response body: { "id": 10, "title": "Flutter Assignment", "completed": false }, explain what each field means and what data type it is (number, string, boolean).<br><br><em><strong>Hint:</strong> Focus on understanding how JSON represents different data types.</em>

Ans :-

  "id": 10,
  "title": "Flutter Assignment",
  "completed": false

  id: The value 10 is a number. It uniquely identifies the assignment.
  title: The value "Flutter Assignment" is a string because it is text enclosed in double quotes. It represents the name of the assignment.
  completed: The value false is a boolean. A boolean can only have one of two values: true or false. Here, 
             false indicates that the assignment has not been completed yet.
